From baef11f99d8c6c7a02533fa55a1a72462ede185a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yolobox <yolobox@phaer.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:30:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kbuild: add build system and linux-kernel package

Add kbuild build system for Linux kernel builds with:
- Configure phase: defconfig + fragment merge + olddefconfig + verification
- Build phase: make with LLVM=1 LLVM_IAS=1
- Install phase: vmlinuz, System.map, config to lib/modules/<version>/

Add linux-kernel 6.18.60 LTS with server config:
- Monolithic (CONFIG_MODULES=n)
- virtio, nvme, ahci storage
- ext4, btrfs, erofs filesystems
- Device mapper (verity, crypt, integrity)
- systemd requirements (cgroups, namespaces, etc.)
- Embedded config (IKCONFIG=y)

Add supporting packages:
- bc: gavinhoward/bc 7.1.0 (replaces GNU bc, no ed dependency)
- elfutils: 0.192 with relocatable patch for objtool

Build workarounds:
- Use UNWINDER_FRAME_POINTER instead of ORC to avoid pthread/libunwind
  RPATH issues with jig's build-time tools
- elfutils: disable make-debug-archive script (hardcoded paths)

Tested: boots in QEMU with minimal initramfs, prints 'golconda kernel ok'
Signed-off-by: yolobox <yolobox@phaer.org>
